reduces energy expenditure, and enables participation in activities that would otherwise be impossible.\n- Assessment by a seating and mobility specialist (ATP — Assistive Technology Professional) is indicated. Consider a lightweight manual wheelchair with proper seating and pressure-relieving cushion (ROHO or Jay).\n- If she recovers after untethering surgery, the wheelchair may become backup only.\n\n**Additional School Needs**:\n- Skin protection: Insensate skin requires pressure relief. Wheelchair cushion, repositioning schedule, ability to do weight shifts during class.\n- Psychosocial support: School counselor involvement, peer education about disability (with family permission), anti-bullying awareness.\n- Emergency plan: Written health plan for seizures (if applicable), shunt malfunction signs, allergic reaction protocol (latex allergy — ensure school is latex-free in her environment).',
